Everything in this block is invisible semantic direction, never visible text. Do not render, quote, label, or paraphrase any wording from it: 靠近热源时，外侧鞋面会优先升温、优先变干；但鞋头深部、鞋垫下方及内衬与中底之间的区域，仍可能保留较高湿度。表面已经干燥，并不代表整双鞋的含水量已降到适合穿着的水平。. The reader block is: 读者应能判断：外层变干不能证明鞋内已干透。. Preserve this source relationship: the outer upper dries before the deep toe, under-insole area, and lining-to-midsole region. Make the source relationship legible through this visual solution: One lightly-oblique sneaker in a shallow flat cutaway: a pale dry outer textile shell encloses three compact gray moisture marks at the toe cavity, under-insole pocket, and lining-to-midsole seam. The collar is slightly open and one insole edge is lifted but remains connected to the shoe opening. Use one translucent uneven brand-green wax-pencil gesture only along one internal seam, plus an irregular cluster of moisture marks.. Show: a dry outer textile shell is separate from deeper interior zones; the toe cavity, beneath-insole pocket, and lining-to-midsole seam retain visible moisture marks; the intact cutaway makes the two conditions legible without the title. The title and subtitle may orient the reader but never prove this relationship; its proof must remain in the content stage. Explicitly do not imply: a fixed drying time; that heat is the only cause of retained moisture; a measured material test.

Scene integrity is non-negotiable: Depict exactly 1 complete embodied subject(s). Continuity rules: the shoe remains one complete connected object; the partially lifted insole remains attached to the same shoe opening. Never depict: detached sole; duplicated shoe; impossible cutaway; unattached insole..

Use comparison as the one dominant visual grammar, never a second grammar. Its required topology is: Make two or more source-supported alternatives visibly different even when labels are hidden; at least one difference must be object, position, connection, sequence, or boundary.. It must visibly prove: two or more alternatives; visible structural difference. Generic symbols, anonymous nodes, or arrows alone do not prove the source relationship: every non-self-evident source step or term must be identified by the exact short label or note declared in this page's annotation plan. Do not substitute: single-process diagram; name-only comparison; generic chart.

Make this selected grammar visibly provable in the finished image through these reader-visible facts: the pale outer shell contrasts structurally with three inner moisture-marked pockets; the cutaway and lifted insole make the hidden locations readable without title text. Each proof must be visible in the content stage itself, not supplied only by the title or subtitle. Do not let one generic illustrative scene substitute for this evidence.

Make these source-supported comparison differences visibly distinct in objects, positions, connections, sequence, or boundaries: the outer upper is dry while three deep interior zones retain moisture marks; the shoe structure visibly separates the dry exterior from the wet interior.

Apply only this page's declared information encoding:
- label targets pale outer textile shell; render exactly once "表层先干"; source support: 外侧鞋面会优先升温、优先变干
- leader targets pale outer textile shell; render no text; source support: 外侧鞋面会优先升温、优先变干
- label targets three internal moisture pockets; render exactly once "深处仍湿"; source support: 鞋头深部、鞋垫下方及内衬与中底之间的区域，仍可能保留较高湿度
- leader targets three internal moisture pockets; render no text; source support: 鞋头深部、鞋垫下方及内衬与中底之间的区域，仍可能保留较高湿度
Render every declared visible label or note exactly once, even if its target groups multiple objects or regions. Use the label role only at 22px with 28px line height: quiet neutral sans-serif, medium, #515151, at most 1 line. Use the note role only at 17px with 23px line height: quiet neutral sans-serif, regular italic, #6B6B6B, at most 1 line. When a declared `label` and `note` have the same target, render them as one two-level callout: the exact label first, then the exact note directly beneath it in the declared note role. They share one local leader; never place either in a card, caption block, or separate detached text area. Its visual language is: Use quiet thin gray leaders and labels; one declared green relation line may be used. Render only the exact visible label or note content declared by the page plan. Annotations are subordinate to the relationship and never decorative. Do not add any annotation not declared here.

Create a single explanatory body image. Render exactly once in the pure-white upper title region: 外干，不等于内干. Use the core-title role only at 48px with 60px line height: high-contrast Songti-like editorial serif, semibold, #1A6B3A, at most 1 line, center aligned around the title-region center at x=600; never left or right align it. Render exactly once directly below it: 表层先干，深处仍可能潮湿. Use the subtitle role only at 28px with 36px line height: high-contrast Songti-like editorial serif, regular, #6B6B6B, at most 1 line, center aligned around that same center; never left or right align it. Treat the two lines as one centered text block. Keep this title region free of artwork, frame, and divider.

Keep all semantic elements inside one calm, asymmetric content cluster with 68–78% quiet space, no more than 4 semantic groups, and 0–3 supporting elements. Treat this as a hard layout constraint, not a preference: the full drawn cluster is a small editorial vignette surrounded by white paper. Vary the related objects' scale, spacing, and vertical placement; do not arrange them as an even row, mirrored pair, grid, card wall, or unrelated decorative collage. The drawn cluster occupies at most 44% of the content-stage width and 44% of its height. Use a small hero scale: scale down objects instead of enlarging one central object to explain internal detail; do not let a cutaway, product, person, or other primary object fill the lower content stage, reach the stage edges, or occupy more than two thirds of the cluster. Keep any declared labels and explanations local and subordinate. Split the page instead of adding competing structures when the relationship cannot remain legible. Do not use edge-to-edge hero; oversized object; lower-stage fill; large cutaway hero or dashboard; card wall; unrelated scenery; logo reserve content.

